--
-- Off-budget armor system: item_armor_curve, item_armor_slot_mult,
-- item_armor_quality_mult. See docs/itemization-changes.md §9.3.
--
-- Armor (the flat ItemTemplate::Armor field on armor-class items) is not
-- part of the percentage-allocated stat budget -- confirmed empirically:
-- for a fixed (ItemLevel, armor class, slot, quality), every single Epic
-- item in item_template carries the exact same Armor value regardless of
-- how wildly its stat distribution varies (a tank-stat piece and a
-- caster-stat piece at the same ilvl/slot/class have identical Armor).
-- Blizzard computed it from a closed-form formula, not per-item authoring,
-- and it never traded off against the stat budget the way Stamina turned
-- out to (§4.5's revision-2 note). Handled the same way as Stamina in
-- every other respect: an off-budget curve, applied at materialization
-- time, with a free per-item `armor_delta` override (item_budget_assign,
-- §3) for authored "texture" -- unlike stamina_delta/dps_delta, it is NOT
-- funded from the item's budget, matching the zero real-world correlation
-- between Armor and stat budget.
--
-- item_armor_curve: median Armor at the Chest/Robe reference slot, Epic
-- quality, one curve per armor class (1=Cloth, 2=Leather, 3=Mail,
-- 4=Plate), sample-size-weighted isotonic regression + interpolation,
-- ilvl 1-300, same method as item_budget_curve (§4.5). PvP season gear
-- (Gladiator/Marshal/Warlord/etc. sets) was excluded from the fit, same
-- reasoning as ilvl 219's exclusion from the main budget curve: it
-- deliberately carries inflated stats/armor relative to PvE loot at the
-- same nominal item level, and left in, it forces the fit to pool through
-- several item levels of raid content at an inflated value it never
-- earned.
--
-- item_armor_slot_mult / item_armor_quality_mult: median ratio of every
-- other slot/quality to the Chest/Robe & Epic reference, across the same
-- dataset. Confirmed both ratios are consistent across all four armor
-- classes (a single shared per-slot and per-quality scale, not one per
-- class) -- exact clean fractions for slot (13/16, 3/4, 9/16, 7/8, 11/16,
-- 7/16, 5/8, 1/2), confirming these come from a formula too. Deliberately
-- separate tables from item_slot_mult/item_quality_mult (the stat-budget
-- versions) -- the ratios do not match; e.g. Wrist is 0.5625 of the stat
-- budget's reference slot but 0.4375 of Armor's.
--
-- baseline_armor = item_armor_curve(ItemLevel, armor_class)
--                   * item_armor_slot_mult(InventoryType)
--                   * item_armor_quality_mult(Quality)
-- final_armor = baseline_armor + armor_delta
--
-- Materialization only touches Armor for items whose class/subclass has a
-- curve entry (armor-class items: Cloth/Leather/Mail/Plate). Shields
-- (subclass 6) and other Armor-class-but-non-wearable-armor items (rings,
-- necks, trinkets, off-hand frills -- subclass 0) have no curve entry and
-- are deliberately left untouched, same as every unassigned item.
--

DELETE FROM `item_armor_slot_mult` WHERE `inv_type` BETWEEN 1 AND 26;

DELETE FROM `item_armor_quality_mult` WHERE `quality` BETWEEN 0 AND 5;

DELETE FROM `item_armor_curve` WHERE `ilvl` BETWEEN 1 AND 300;
